            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Sanskrit for a drought, then the Sanskrit for remedies."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: योग्यः",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "योग्यः — yogyaḥ — \"qualified; fit\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "यदि अरुणः योग्यः अस्ति, तर्हि सः नायकः भवेत्। yadi aruṇaḥ yogyaḥ asti, tarhi saḥ nāyakaḥ bhavet. If Arun is qualified, he should be the leader."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "योग्यः (yogyaḥ) is built on yoga, \"a yoking, union\", from the root √yuj, \"to join\"; MW gives yogya \"fit for the yoke\" and \"useful, proper, qualified, able\" (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
